Similarly for y.

- Rule weights: w(i,j) = μ_i(x) * μ_j(y). The rule matrix: rows i = N, Z, P for x; columns j = N, Z, P for y.

Outputs c(i,j):
   N x N -> -30
   N x Z -> -20
   N x P -> -10
   Z x N -> -10
   Z x Z -> 0
   Z x P -> 10
   P x N -> 10
   P x Z -> 20
